                <h2>Why Balance Alerts Are Critical to Campaign Success</h2>
<p>A utility app's overseas team once experienced an 8-hour campaign pause due to account balance depletion during nighttime hours. Since peak conversions coincided with this period, their CPA increased by approximately 35% and daily ROI dropped by 12 percentage points. This case demonstrates that balance management is not just a financial concern but a core operational issue directly affecting campaign performance.</p>
<h2>5-Step Checklist to Prevent Delivery Interruption</h2>
<h3>Step 1: Set Multi-Tier Alert Thresholds</h3>
<ul>
<li>Base alert: triggered when balance falls below 2x daily spend</li>
<li>Urgent alert: triggered when balance falls below 0.5x daily spend</li>
<li>Advance alert: notification when budget reaches 80% consumption</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Checklist:</strong> Has each account been configured with at least two alert levels? Are notifications sent to multiple team members?</p>
<h3>Step 2: Configure Auto-Recharge Policies</h3>
<ul>
<li>Link credit card or PayPal as backup payment method</li>
<li>Set auto-recharge trigger conditions (e.g., auto-top-up when balance falls below threshold)</li>
<li>Establish single recharge limits to prevent overspending</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Checklist:</strong> Has auto-recharge been tested? Are payment methods still valid?</p>
<h3>Step 3: Build Balance Health Monitoring Dashboard</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Monitoring Dimension</th>
<th>Indicator</th>
<th>Warning Value</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Spend Velocity</td>
<td>Daily spend trend</td>
<td>Sudden 20%+ change</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Balance Adequacy</td>
<td>Balance/Daily Spend</td>
<td>Below 3 days</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Recharge Timeliness</td>
<td>Recharge arrival time</td>
<td>Over 2 hours</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Checklist:</strong> Is the monitoring dashboard checked daily? Is there someone responsible for follow-ups on anomalies?</p>
<h3>Step 4: Establish Exception Response SOP</h3>
<ol>
<li>Confirm account status within 5 minutes of alert trigger</li>
<li>Immediately initiate manual recharge or enable auto-recharge if balance is insufficient</li>
<li>Verify all ad groups are running normally after recharge arrival</li>
<li>If recharge delays exceed 30 minutes, contact agent or platform support</li>
<li>Document interruption duration and impact data post-incident</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Checklist:</strong> Is the SOP documented in writing? Are all team members familiar with the process?</p>
<h3>Step 5: Review and Optimize Alert Mechanisms</h3>
<ul>
<li>Weekly review of alert triggers and root causes</li>
<li>Analyze spend fluctuation patterns to adjust alert thresholds</li>
<li>Evaluate recharge channel stability and optimize backup plans</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Checklist:</strong> Is there a regular review habit? Are thresholds updated with business changes?</p>
<h2>Quick FAQ</h2>
<p><strong>Q: How to monitor balances across multiple accounts?</strong><br />
Consider using third-party management tools or building an internal dashboard to centralize all account balances and alert statuses.</p>
<p><strong>Q: What if auto-recharge fails?</strong><br />
Ensure backup payment methods are valid while retaining manual recharge as an emergency option.</p>
<p><strong>Q: How to handle nighttime balance risks with cross-timezone teams?</strong><br />
Set up on-call notifications covering all global time zones to ensure response availability at any hour.</p>
